#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# golden_ratio

#% text
# `golden_ratio` is the golden ratio `(1 + sqrt(5))/2 = 1.6180...`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `golden_ratio` is exact and known to be a positive real; `n(golden_ratio, d)` gives `d` digits.

#% item
# It satisfies `golden_ratio^2 == golden_ratio + 1`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
golden_ratio
#% output
#= golden_ratio

#% cell
n(golden_ratio)
#% output
#= 1.618033988749895

#% cell
n(golden_ratio, 40)
#% output
#= 1.61803398874989484820458683436563811772030918

#% cell
n(fibonacci(40)/fibonacci(39), 15)
#% output
#= 1.6180339887498947364

#% cell
simplify(golden_ratio^2 - golden_ratio - 1)
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fibonacci`, `catalan`, `euler_gamma`
